## 1.2. "Educational Purpose"

"Educational Purpose" means a genuine activity whose primary purpose is to study, learn, teach, demonstrate, experiment with, analyze, or evaluate software, programming, computer science, software engineering, system administration, cybersecurity, architecture, APIs, infrastructure, or related technical concepts.

Educational Purposes include, without limitation:

- studying and reading the source code;
- analyzing the implementation of the Software;
- understanding its architecture;
- studying its algorithms;
- studying its APIs;
- studying its dependencies;
- studying its protocols;
- studying its security properties;
- studying its design decisions;
- explaining the Software to students or learners;
- demonstrating the Software;
- using the Software as teaching material;
- using the Software during a course;
- using the Software during a workshop;
- using the Software during a laboratory exercise;
- creating exercises based on the Software;
- completing exercises based on the Software;
- modifying the Software as part of an exercise;
- debugging the Software;
- intentionally introducing errors or vulnerabilities for educational purposes;
- fixing errors or vulnerabilities;
- replacing components;
- removing components;
- migrating away from the Software;
- migrating to the Software;
- reproducing a real-world technical scenario;
- simulating a production environment;
- testing deployment procedures;
- testing migration procedures;
- testing upgrade procedures;
- testing rollback procedures;
- testing failure and recovery procedures;
- testing integrations;
- benchmarking;
- conducting technical experiments;
- comparing the Software with other technologies;
- creating educational demonstrations;
- creating examinations or assignments;
- creating technical training exercises.

An activity does not cease to be an Educational Purpose merely because it uses realistic infrastructure, realistic data structures, production-like environments, real-world scenarios, or professional development techniques.

