# 29. Interpretation

This License is intended to permit genuine educational use while preventing commercial, professional, operational, production, resale, redistribution, and service-based exploitation of the Software.

Where an activity contains both educational and non-educational elements, the overall purpose and substance of the activity shall be considered.

An educational component does not automatically make an otherwise prohibited activity an Educational Purpose.

For example, the following remain prohibited:

- using the Software in production while training employees on it;
- using the Software for a customer while teaching employees how it works;
- using the Software commercially while conducting occasional demonstrations;
- using the Software in a commercial product and providing educational documentation;
- using the Software to provide a paid service while describing the service as educational;
- deploying the Software operationally and characterizing the deployment as a practical exercise.

The educational purpose must be genuine and primary.

